Model Context Protocol (MCP)
=============================

Canonical git repository:
	https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol

Local path:
	ref/mcp (git submodule)

This metadata file:
	ref/mcp.SOURCE (sibling of the submodule directory; not inside it)

Pin recorded in this tree:
	Tag:    2026-07-28
	Commit: 5f5440bb26a62e2cf3440b92da5a667efa03b267

Why this pin:
	Specification 0015 cites the Model Context Protocol revision dated
	2026-07-28. That date is a tag on the publisher repository. The
	submodule is pinned to that tag, not to the moving default branch.
	The older GitHub path modelcontextprotocol/specification resolves to
	this same repository. It is not a separate publisher and it is not
	a mirror that someone else maintains.

Form:
	Form 1 git submodule from the publisher repository that maintains
	the Model Context Protocol specification and schema.

License:
	The upstream LICENSE file at this pin says the project is moving
	from the MIT License to Apache License 2.0. New code and
	specification contributions are Apache 2.0. Documentation
	contributions, other than specifications, are CC-BY-4.0.
	Contributions that were MIT and have not been relicensed stay MIT.
	The same file then includes the Apache License 2.0 text. Surmount
	does not own that text. This repository's Unlicense does not
	relicense the pin. See ref/README.md and ref/mcp/LICENSE.

How to re-check the pin (from repo root; requires git permission when used
by an agent):
	1. git -C ref/mcp describe --tags --always
	2. git -C ref/mcp rev-parse HEAD

Do not edit files inside this submodule. Cite the tag and commit instead.
Do not place Surmount-only metadata inside the submodule working tree.
Canonical upstream URL remains first-class; the submodule freezes the
reviewed pin for this repository.

TOON, as specification 0015 uses that name, is the notation the product
names through util/toon. ACP, as that specification uses that name, is
the internal agent client protocol inside grok-oss. Neither is this
Model Context Protocol pin.
